# The pinned dnscrypt-proxy source, and the digest it has to carry.
#
# dnscrypt-proxy is not a dependency of this package: the binary is built from
# source into the package, so there is a source tree to pin. scripts/build-deb.sh
# verifies the line below against the archive it was given BEFORE it extracts
# anything, and it never builds a tree whose archive does not match, so a swapped
# archive fails the build rather than producing a resolver this project did not
# review.
#
# The archive is the upstream tag's tarball, unmodified:
#
#   curl -L -o build/dnscrypt-proxy-2.1.18.tar.gz \
#     https://github.com/DNSCrypt/dnscrypt-proxy/archive/refs/tags/2.1.18.tar.gz
#
# `sha256sum -c packaging/debian/dnscrypt-proxy.sha256` from the repository root
# checks a copy already placed in build/.
#
# The tag's COMMIT is recorded as well as the archive's digest, and it is not a
# checksum: it is `git ls-remote https://github.com/DNSCrypt/dnscrypt-proxy
# refs/tags/2.1.18` from the same fetch. A digest proves the archive is the same
# bytes every time and says nothing about whether those bytes are what the tag
# points at today, so a future divergence is attributable to a RE-TAG (which moves
# this SHA) rather than to a transport change (which would not) -- and a re-tag is a
# change somebody has to look at, not one a pin silently absorbs. Neither number is a
# signature; see the task report's NOT VERIFIED list.
tag-commit: 30c0a9e91c12a15c081ac90546dd657c4ab98fbc
